text:
marta: quick QA pass on the 'moonbeam' dark palette mock. main asks: legend legibility on compact sparkline rows, caret color in inline code, and theme selector copy. figma: https://figma.com/file/moonbeam (frames 2-4). please skim.

liam: nice direction. tiny legends lose separation at 320px; colored swatches blend into the bg. suggest 1px white halo (rgba(255,255,255,0.06)) + increase dot area to 10px.

kai: caret color: using --code-caret: #5dd3ff on #0b1220 feels low contrast when caret sits over punctuation. propose #9befff for caret and keep block bg darker. also inline-code weight 500 helps punctuation.

reena: copy: agree with explicit label. propose "Theme: System (default) / Light / Dark". add aria-label: "Theme preference: follows OS when System selected" for screen readers.

marta: good. small chart suggestion: introduce an accessible series set for colorblind modes: primary #2fb7ff, alt #ffb86b, spare #b48df3. add pattern fill fallback for exports.

kai: quick CSS tokens snippet:

```
--surface: #0b1220;
--code-bg: #0f1722;
--code-text: #cfe7ff;
--code-caret: #9befff;
--legend-halo: rgba(255,255,255,0.06);
--series-1: #2fb7ff;
--series-2: #ffb86b;
```

liam: will run contrast checks. also recommend tooltip change: when value is sampled, show "value (sampled)" not just "value". reduces support confusion.

reena: accessibility nit: focus ring should be 2px with visible offset on compact rows. don't rely solely on color change.

marta: i'll open a tiny PR that updates tokens, the toggle copy, and tooltips. @design-bot can you create a deploy preview?

design-bot: created preview: https://deploy.preview/redwood-console/feat/moonbeam-theme (expires in 48h). automated axe: 2 violations (caret contrast, legend halo missing). Details posted to PR.

liam: :thumbsup: i'll post contrast screenshots when done.

reena: tagging infra for token rename to semantic names before merge.

marta: thanks team — aiming to merge after fixes. :rocket:
